                <pb facs="0181" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/1046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-26T12:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1934—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Press reports from London have stated that the British Government has
                    instructed the British Ambassador that, in case Pu Yi makes an official visit to
                    Tokyo and invitations are issued for attendance at functions in his honor, the
                    Ambassador is not to attend.</p>
                <p>In case any such situation develops, please report immediately the facts and add
                    your comments, thus enabling the Department to give you appropriate
                    instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
